&lt;p&gt;Keeping recovery information updated can make account recovery easier when unexpected problems occur.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Review Account Security Activity&lt;br&gt;
Security activity can provide useful information about how an account has been accessed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users should pay attention to unexpected events, especially those they do not recognize.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Potential warning signs can include:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Unknown login activity&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Unfamiliar devices&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Unexpected password changes&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Unrecognized security notifications&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Changes to recovery information&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Unusual account behavior&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If suspicious activity is detected, the account should be secured promptly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Manage Devices Used With Yahoo&lt;br&gt;
An established Yahoo account may have been accessed from many devices over the years.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Some devices may no longer be in use.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users should periodically review the devices associated with their account and remove access that is no longer necessary where Yahoo provides that capability.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is particularly useful after:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Buying a new phone&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Replacing a computer&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Selling an old device&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Losing a device&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Using a shared computer&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Recovering an account&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Keeping device access under control can reduce unnecessary exposure.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Protect Your Yahoo Inbox&lt;br&gt;
The inbox may contain important personal or professional information.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users should avoid leaving sensitive information unnecessarily exposed and should be careful when responding to unknown senders.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Important messages can be organized into folders or other available categories.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Examples of useful organization groups include:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Personal&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Work&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Finance&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Shopping&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Travel&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Education&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Subscriptions&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Important documents&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An organized inbox makes it easier to locate information later.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Managing Old Yahoo Emails&lt;br&gt;
Long-term email accounts can accumulate thousands of messages.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not every old message needs to remain in the inbox.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users can review older messages and decide whether they should be:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Kept&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Archived&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Organized&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Downloaded where appropriate&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Deleted&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Important records should be preserved carefully before unnecessary messages are removed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A simple cleanup routine can make the inbox considerably easier to manage.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reduce Unwanted Subscriptions&lt;br&gt;
Newsletters and promotional emails can gradually fill an old Yahoo inbox.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Over time, users may subscribe to websites that they no longer use.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Unsubscribing from unnecessary mailing lists can reduce clutter and make important emails easier to identify.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users should be cautious when interacting with unfamiliar unsubscribe links. When a message appears suspicious, it may be safer to manage subscriptions directly through the relevant legitimate service.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Protect Against Phishing Emails&lt;br&gt;
Phishing is an important concern for every email user.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A phishing message may attempt to convince someone that an urgent action is required.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example, a fraudulent email may claim that:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The account will be closed&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A payment failed&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A security issue was detected&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A password must be confirmed&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A package is waiting&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A verification process is required&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users should carefully inspect unexpected messages before clicking links or entering information.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Important warning signs include unusual sender addresses, unexpected attachments, urgent language, suspicious links, and requests for passwords or verification codes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Do Not Share Passwords or Verification Codes&lt;br&gt;
Passwords and verification codes should remain private.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Legitimate services generally have specific procedures for account security and recovery. Users should be cautious if someone contacts them unexpectedly and asks for login credentials or verification information.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A verification code should never be shared simply because another person claims to need it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Keeping these details private is one of the simplest ways to reduce account-security risks.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Managing Yahoo Contacts&lt;br&gt;
An established Yahoo account may contain a large contact list accumulated over several years.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Some contacts may still be important, while others may be outdated.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reviewing contacts periodically can help keep communication organized.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users can identify:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Important personal contacts&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Professional contacts&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Outdated addresses&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Duplicate information&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Contacts that are no longer relevant&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Keeping a clean contact list can improve the overall email experience.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yahoo Accounts for Personal Communication&lt;br&gt;
Many people use Yahoo Mail for personal communication.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An established personal account may contain years of conversations with family, friends, organizations, and services.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Because personal messages can contain private information, account security should be taken seriously.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users should also review old messages and attachments periodically to determine whether any information should be retained, archived, or removed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yahoo Accounts for Professional Communication&lt;br&gt;
Email remains an important part of professional communication.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A Yahoo account may be used for:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Business correspondence&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Freelance communication&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Job-related communication&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Service registrations&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Client messages&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Professional subscriptions&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For professional use, organization and security are especially important.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users should keep important correspondence easy to find and should avoid mixing sensitive professional information with unnecessary promotional messages when possible.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Privacy Management&lt;br&gt;
Privacy should be reviewed regularly because online circumstances can change.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Information that was appropriate to share years ago may no longer be relevant today.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users should review:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Account information&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Recovery details&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Connected services&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Email forwarding&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Filters&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Device access&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Contacts&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Stored messages&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The objective is to maintain control over personal information and reduce unnecessary exposure.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Check Email Forwarding and Filters&lt;br&gt;
Email forwarding and filters can be useful tools for managing messages.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;However, old settings can sometimes remain active long after they are needed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users should review these settings periodically to ensure that messages are being handled as expected.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An old forwarding destination that is no longer controlled by the user could create an unnecessary privacy concern.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Likewise, an outdated filter could automatically move important messages into an unexpected folder.&lt;/p&gt;

